# 20 — Terrain layers and holes

Read `thinking-12-terrain-layers-and-holes.md` and its phase 16/18 references. Orlando authorized implementation on 2026-11-05 and confirmed volume/surface intersection for holes.

## Scope and decisions

- 20.1: existing Unity Colors mappings gain an optional TerrainLayer reference. External assets are read-only; generated fallback is explicitly matte. Preserve claims, local drift, legacy baselines and Undo.
- 20.2: existing untilted box/cylinder/free-form Hole shapes inside a terrain source group cut only its owning terrain. Height operations run first, holes union afterwards. No hole Fade. External scene holes, entity/array cutters and terrain-aware gameplay queries remain deferred.
- Derive one presence value per terrain cell, shared by preview/capture, picking, GLB and Unity. Prototype center sampling against volume intersection; document sub-cell limits. Canonical resolution is retained during edits to terrains containing holes so entrances do not disappear into a coarse drag grid.
- Explicitly version exported mask data; preserve reading of old exports and protect Unity-painted holes. No scene sample arrays are persisted.

## Required checks

- Unit/store tests: containment, hidden inputs, source-only scope, taper/bevel, final heights, cell boundaries, picking, edit/undo/copy, export row reversal/revisions and GLB empty/partial masks.
- `npm test`, `npm run typecheck`, web build, `scripts/compile-unity.sh`, diff check.
- Scratch browser: author/edit/hide/delete/undo holes, clean capture, terrain picking; never use main scene data.
- Scratch Unity: real importer map/change/clear, matte settings, external assets unchanged, legacy migration, claims/drift, mask/collider orientation, last-hole removal, Undo/Redo/save/reload and compatibility. Reuse existing terrain regression harness.
- Human acceptance remains Orlando's visual check in his project; automated checks do not substitute for it.

